---
title: Choosing and wiring an agent-operable web UI layer
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Choosing and wiring an agent-operable web UI layer
  accDescr: Classify each route as content-first or interactive. Content routes stop at crawlable HTML, sitemap, and Schema.org JSON-LD. Light forms add declarative WebMCP attributes. Interactive apps feature-detect document.modelContext or wire a structured bridge such as UI SDK createAgent, then guard mutations with allow hooks and server authorization.
  start["Classify the web surface"]
  static["Content / brochure / docs route\n(web-crawlability only; mark Band B N/A)"]
  forms["Light form workflows\nDeclarative WebMCP\n(<form toolname tooldescription>)"]
  app["Interactive SPA / SaaS app"]
  plain["Plain WebMCP\ndocument.modelContext.registerTool()"]
  sdk["Behavior + bridge library\ne.g. UI SDK createAgent() + registerTools()"]
  safety["Safety + provenance\nallow() confirmation on destructive actions\nsource === 'agent' audit + server authz"]
  verify["Verify\nsnapshot / query / act + no-op fallback\nwhen document.modelContext is absent"]

  start -->|"Static / content-first"| static
  start -->|"Simple forms"| forms
  start -->|"Dense interactive state"| app
  app -->|"Existing UI kit"| plain
  app -->|"New or cross-framework primitives"| sdk
  forms --> safety
  plain --> safety
  sdk --> safety
  safety --> verify

  class start success
  class static primary
  class forms,app,plain,sdk secondary
  class safety warning
  class verify primary
